---
import '@/styles/global.css';
import Consent from '@/components/Consent.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" class="dark scroll-smooth">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <Consent />
    <title>Privacy Policy — StealthVault</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Privacy policy for the StealthVault iOS and Android app." />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://snazzie.space/stealthvault/privacy/" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
  </head>
  <body class="bg-background text-foreground antialiased">
    <header class="pointer-events-none fixed inset-x-0 top-0 z-50 flex justify-center pt-4 px-4">
      <nav class="pointer-events-auto flex items-center gap-1 rounded-full border border-border bg-card/80 px-2 py-1.5 backdrop-blur-md w-full max-w-2xl">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 px-3 text-sm font-semibold text-foreground shrink-0">
          <a href="/stealthvault/" aria-label="StealthVault, home" class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="size-2 rounded-full bg-foreground" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            StealthVault
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="ml-auto flex items-center gap-0.5">
          <a href="/stealthvault/faq/" class="rounded-full px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-muted-foreground transition-colors hover:bg-white/10 hover:text-foreground">FAQ</a>
          <a href="/stealthvault/privacy/" class="rounded-full px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-muted-foreground transition-colors hover:bg-white/10 hover:text-foreground">Privacy</a>
          <a href="/stealthvault/terms/" class="rounded-full px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-muted-foreground transition-colors hover:bg-white/10 hover:text-foreground">Terms</a>
        </div>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 pb-24 pt-28">
      <div class="mb-8">
        <a href="/stealthvault/" class="text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground transition-colors">← Back</a>
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground text-sm mb-10">StealthVault · Last updated June 3, 2025</p>

      <div class="prose prose-invert prose-sm max-w-none space-y-8 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-3">Overview</h2>
          <p>
            StealthVault is a private, encrypted media vault. <strong class="text-foreground">Your vault content</strong> — photos, videos, albums, tags, and browsing data — is encrypted on your device and never leaves it unless you explicitly initiate a device-to-device sync or portal session on your local network. We never transmit your media to external servers.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            To keep the app stable and free, we use two third-party services from Google that collect limited, non-content data: <strong class="text-foreground">Firebase Crashlytics</strong> (crash and diagnostic data) and <strong class="text-foreground">Google AdMob</strong> (advertising). These are described below. They never receive your vault content.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-3">Data Stored on Your Device</h2>
          <p>The following data is stored <strong class="text-foreground">locally on your device only</strong>, encrypted at rest:</p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5">
            <li>Media files (photos and videos) you import into the vault</li>
            <li>Album names and organization</li>
            <li>Tags and metadata you assign to media</li>
            <li>Browser history and bookmarks from the in-app browser</li>
            <li>Your vault passcode (stored as a derived key — never in plaintext)</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-3">Encryption</h2>
          <p>
            Media is encrypted with AES using a random data encryption key (DEK) that is itself wrapped by a key derived from your passcode. The DEK is held in memory only while the vault is unlocked and is zeroed out on lock. Encrypted blobs are stored in the app's private documents directory — inaccessible to other apps.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-3">Network Access</h2>
          <p>StealthVault requests network access for two optional features only:</p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5">
            <li>
              <strong class="text-foreground">Web Portal</strong> — starts a local HTTP server on your device so you can access your vault from a browser on the same Wi-Fi network. No data is routed through the internet.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-foreground">Device Sync</strong> — transfers encrypted media between two devices on the same local network using a pairing code. No data is routed through the internet.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Both features are opt-in and off by default. Neither transmits data to any external server.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-3">In-App Browser</h2>
          <p>
            The built-in browser is a WebView with ad blocking. It does not use a proxy or VPN — it makes requests directly from your device. Browsing history and bookmarks are stored locally in the encrypted vault database. No browsing data is sent to us.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-3">Subscriptions</h2>
          <p>
            StealthVault uses <strong class="text-foreground">RevenueCat</strong> to manage in-app subscriptions. RevenueCat processes purchase data through Apple App Store or Google Play. Their privacy policy applies to that transaction data. We receive only an anonymous entitlement status — no payment details.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-3">Crash Reporting</h2>
          <p>
            StealthVault uses <strong class="text-foreground">Firebase Crashlytics</strong> (a Google service) to collect crash reports and diagnostic data so we can fix bugs and improve stability. This may include device model, operating system version, app version, and the technical state of the app at the time of a crash. <strong class="text-foreground">It never includes your vault content</strong> (your media, albums, tags, or browsing data). Crashlytics data is processed by Google under <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-2 hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity">Firebase's privacy and security terms</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-3">Advertising</h2>
          <p>
            StealthVault displays a single banner ad through <strong class="text-foreground">Google AdMob</strong>, configured to request <strong class="text-foreground">non-personalized ads only</strong>. We do not ask for tracking permission and do not use your device's advertising identifier to profile you — the app declares "no tracking" in its iOS privacy manifest. To serve a non-personalized ad, AdMob receives only coarse contextual information (such as approximate region derived from your IP and general device type) and an identifier used for frequency capping and fraud prevention; it is never used to build a profile of you. AdMob never receives your vault content. Google's use of this data is governed by the <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-2 hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity">Google Ads policies</a>. A paid subscription removes ads entirely.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-3">Permissions</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5">
            <li><strong class="text-foreground">Photo Library</strong> — to import media into the vault and optionally delete originals after import.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-foreground">Camera</strong> — to capture media directly into the vault (if implemented).</li>
            <li><strong class="text-foreground">Face ID / Biometrics</strong> — to unlock the vault without typing your passcode. Biometric data never leaves the device's secure enclave.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-foreground">Local Network</strong> — for the Web Portal and Device Sync features.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-3">Age Requirement</h2>
          <p>
            StealthVault is intended for adults aged 18 and over and is rated 17+. The app is not directed at anyone under 18, and we do not knowingly collect information from anyone under 18.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-3">Changes</h2>
          <p>
            If this policy changes materially, the updated date above will reflect that. Continued use of the app after changes constitutes acceptance.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-3">Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Questions? Email <a href="mailto:acoop133@hotmail.com" class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-2 hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity">acoop133@hotmail.com</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

      </div>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
